WEBVTT

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.310
Good thing we made it in time!

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:30.110
There's no puzzle I can't
solve! Let’s move on!

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.200
Huh? Hey, let’s take a break!

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.320
I swear I will defeat Orpheus!

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.080
And I WILL get Jin back!

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:16.990
Because You Were Watching

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.500
Welcome to the Republic of Amgine.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:52.400
I’ve heard he wishes to
welcome you as national guests.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.590
So now you’re President
Enigma’s representative?

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.130
Looks like someone’s come up in the
world when we weren’t looking.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:04.530
She was kind enough to pick us up,
so do you really have to snap at her?

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:09.900
Antoinette, I said you could tag along,
but we’re not here to sightsee.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.920
I’ll have you remember that I’m the one
who bought the tickets to Amgine.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.650
Yeah, you did. Thanks.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.940
Wow! This isn’t bad!

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.970
Dinner is at 5:00.

00:03:37.210 --> 00:03:39.570
We have bedrooms prepared for both of you.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.540
Your clothes are over here.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.490
Wear whatever you like.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:49.850
Wow! There are even clothes for me!

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:54.150
That’s no big! It just goes to show
he knew we were coming!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.910
Can you hear me, Jin Makata--no, Orpheus?

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:12.330
You already know why I’m here, don’t you?

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:15.670
Then drop the act and show yourself!

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:17.600
Let’s get the ball rolling!

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.300
Galileo!

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:23.880
Well, we can talk over
dinner. I’ll send for you.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.680
Raetsel!

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:32.100
Kaito was worried about you,
even after all that’s happen.

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.060
He should worry about himself.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.680
I will admit that man is driven.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:57.460
However, he could not hold
a candle to Kaito Daimon.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.010
Gammon went to the Republic of Amgine?!

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.910
Yeah. Please look at this.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.910
We have already confirmed that
they arrived via an Amgine jet.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:18.630
He even took Miss Erena!
This isn’t the time for his games!

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:22.920
He also heard that message Raetsel delivered.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.550
And there’s only one way to save Jin.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.200
What is it?

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:33.200
Me, Kaito, Rook, Freecell and Gammon.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.890
One out of us five must awaken as a Phi-Brain

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:41.350
and offer our brain to Orpheus as his vessel.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.940
If we do, he will release Jin.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.930
Do you think... he is blindly
trying to become a Phi-Bain

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:53.170
simply because his name was
listed amongst the candidates?

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.720
No. He of all people would never do that.

00:05:56.730 --> 00:06:02.580
Right. I imagine Gammon is trying
to become Kaito’s shield.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.880
I swear, how very like Galileo to do that.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.950
But even if that’s his plan,
this gamble is far too risky

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:13.610
for Gammon at his current ability level.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:17.350
One false move could cost him his life!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.300
Does he even stand a chance?

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:25.370
For the time being, we’ll
have to see how things pan out.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:39.370
How does it taste?

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.900
It’s good! There isn’t
any room for complaints.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:50.530
But you can cut the charade!
I’m here to see Orpheus.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.450
How could you say that when
you’re making a pig of yourself?

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.350
Can’t fight on an empty stomach! Seconds!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:00.390
You seem to be rather feisty.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:01.440
Wha--?!

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.160
Jin!

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.860
Orpheus! You bastard!

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:12.870
A lady companion. You must be confident.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.060
Leave Antoinette out of this!

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.120
Puzzles are the issue here!

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:20.890
Weren’t you the one who designated me?

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:22.770
Hurry and get my puzzle ready!

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.110
Don’t be so hasty.

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:30.120
I selected you as a candidate, but ultimately,

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.590
you are no match for Kaito Daimon.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.490
I don’t stand under anyone!

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:37.540
And I’ll prove it to you!

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.850
I, the Great Gammon Sakanoue,
will prove it right this friggin’ second!

00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.670
Wait, Galileo! Calm down!

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:44.360
Shuddup!

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.110
Keep outta this!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.600
Raetsel, good news!

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.120
You may get your Jin back
sooner than I had anticipated.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.640
I shall take this man instead.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:09.520
In that case, Gammon Sakanoue,
I shall grant your wish.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.210
Wh-where is this?!

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.910
Welcome, Gammon Sakanoue!

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:44.160
An Armlet of Orpheus slumbers
in this Philosopher’s Puzzle.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.630
I knew it! You’re planning to...

00:08:53.150 --> 00:08:55.760
Reach the goal on the top floor before the

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.680
last grain of sand in the sandglass drops.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.180
Otherwise, everything will disappear.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.030
All that will await you is
the bottom of this abyss.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.770
I’m the only one challengin’ you!

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:10.440
She doesn’t have anything
to do with this! Let her out!

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.720
It’s too late.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:17.510
Besides, it makes the game more interesting
when two lives are on the line.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:20.600
Bastard! You’re playing dirty!

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:22.180
I’ll be okay.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.180
Wha--?!

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.180
Are you sure?

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:28.400
Galileo, you plan on getting the Armlet

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.270
and turning into a Phi-Brain before
anyone else, don’t you?

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:37.010
You’re trying to protect Kaito Daimon!

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.250
In that case, I’ll stay to see the
strength of your determination!

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.520
Wh-what’s wrong with you?!

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.420
One wrong step and you’re a goner!

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.130
I know that!

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:51.400
No, you don’t!

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:56.370
Buster, if you’re Galileo,
then I’m Antoinette.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:02.910
Do you think I’d ever regret entrusting
my life to a certain puzzle-loving fool?

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.910
Since I’m here, I’m going to watch
you through to the end!

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.570
You’re...

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.740
Do you have time for this?
The puzzle has already begun.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.150
Damn it!

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:29.120
Since there are different colored panels,

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.000
the colors should indicate
different pattern movements.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:33.940
In that case...!

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:39.470
It’s moving! It’s a sliding puzzle!

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.220
Next up is a green panel!

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.140
From the direction of the sandglass,

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:51.960
don’t the blue panels run vertically and
the green panels run horizontally?

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.150
You’ve got it!

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:58.470
Watch your step! If you
fall, it’s all over.

00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:01.670
Puzzle time... Let’s begin!

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:28.620
Blue panels go vertically and green panels
go horizontally, which means...

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:31.690
to go up to the next floor, we need...

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:33.630
Red!

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:35.630
Let’s go!

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:46.220
Just like I thought!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.230
What’s the matter?

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.500
Won’t a red one take us up?

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:01.860
But that one will lead to a dead end.

00:12:04.260 --> 00:12:05.510
This way!

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:16.270
Sure enough, Galileo is
amazing when he’s serious!

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.430
You’re doing great!

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:26.370
This’ll be a breeze!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.490
Tch! How to make a guy feel sick!

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.370
What’s your problem?! And here I
was paying you a compliment!

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.110
I meant this puzzle!

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:38.240
From here, it’s easy
to see where the goal is.

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:41.800
If we can reach the fourth
floor with those red panels,

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.640
we’ll hit the goal! There
aren’t any other routes.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.280
What’s wrong with that?

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.040
Okay, let’s go!

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.130
How foolish.

00:13:03.990 --> 00:13:04.930
Wh-what?!

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.410
H-hey, what gives?!

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.870
He planted a nasty trap!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:12.210
How are we supposed to reach the goal

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:14.940
if you don’t know which
red panels go up or down?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.420
We get to start over from the beginning, eh?

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.540
What’s goin’ on?

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.430
No matter where we go,
it leads to a dead end!

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.970
N-no!

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.300
Show me! How will you handle this,
Gammon Sakanoue?

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:48.090
What on earth should we do?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.200
Don’t move!

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:58.250
What’s your plan?

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:01.340
There is always an answer to every puzzle!

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:04.490
The game has just begun!

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.640
Galileo, time’s running out!

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:37.520
I know!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.960
We’re gonna take a
different route this time.

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:01.540
It worked! We’re on the top floor!

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.170
It’s too soon to start rejoicin’!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.530
It doesn’t...?

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.370
Yeah. I can’t find a route to the goal.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:15.340
What’s goin’ on?!

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:28.440
This is Galileo’s battle.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:32.010
All I can do is watch.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:36.970
No, even if I wanted to help,
I don’t know the answer!

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:41.600
So that’s the best you can do?

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:44.840
You shouldn’t have tried your hand at it.

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.590
You and that lady can spend
all of eternity comforting

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.250
one another at the pit of the abyss.

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.350
Stuff it!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.460
I’m not gonna let things
work out like you expected!

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:02.100
There’s no way I’ll ever give up!

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.500
To reach the blue panel
that connects to the goal,

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:11.030
we gotta return to the third floor.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:16.180
But... there isn’t a route to those
panels on the third floor!

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.350
How are we supposed to reach the goal?

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.490
What’s with that panel?

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.480
Why is there a panel that can’t move?

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:39.160
There’s something about that panel!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.830
Otherwise, there’s no way anyone
could solve this puzzle!

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.050
Let’s go, Erena!

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.820
All right! Gammon, I trust you!

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:03.980
That’s right! I’m Galileo:
The Great Gammon Sakanoue!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.450
So that was the deal.

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:27.350
Over here!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.110
Move it!

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:46.820
Hurry, hurry!

00:17:50.860 --> 00:17:52.250
JUMP!

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:32.880
The Armlet of Orpheus?!

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:42.050
Gammon!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:53.920
It couldn’t be! Did
the Armlet consume him?!

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.440
Congratulations. Just as you so desired,

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:04.060
you have acquired that which
Kaito Daimon possessed.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:09.590
But it would seem the future
I foresaw has come to pass.

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.860
No... You’re lying!

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:15.840
Like that’ll ever happen.

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.770
Save your bullshit!

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:34.500
I’m light years more impressive than Kaito!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:37.730
Oh?

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:40.100
How fascinating!

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:45.220
Whenever Kaito Daimon is involved,
the future instantly begins to sway.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:48.290
Tch! You’ll never get me to buy that!

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.670
Wait, Gammon!

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:55.290
But no matter how much it sways...

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.870
Well, it really wasn’t that tough
for someone with my brains!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.790
You didn’t have to watch me after all!

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.420
Huh? What’s wrong?

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:21.350
Erena?

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:26.830
Wh-what brought that on?!

00:20:27.310 --> 00:20:29.580
Moron! Moron! Moron! MORON!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:34.150
Quit making me constantly worry
about you, you giant moron!

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:40.340
All I could do... was watch.

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.460
I... could only watch...

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:48.930
I’m sorry!

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:55.350
I was able to solve it
’cause you were watching.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:09.490
Hey, didn’t you say my real name
for the first time back there?

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:12.100
Huh? I did?

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:21.050
Moron!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.250
What is this...?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.170
Is something wrong?

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:46.200
What the hell is this?

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:20.120
Gammon?

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:21.820
Gammon?!

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:25.130
Gammon! GAMMON!

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:04.480
I know this seems random, but
here’s a silly question.

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:07.360
Doubt, let’s say there is
a staircase in front of you.

00:24:07.360 --> 00:24:09.210
Does it go up or down?

00:24:10.150 --> 00:24:12.950
I’d like to assume otherwise,
but is this why you summoned me?

00:24:12.950 --> 00:24:13.470
Yep.

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:14.890
You’re wasting my time.

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.330
No, I’m not. I’m giving you a chance!

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:19.770
Get it right and I’ll let
you appear on the show.

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:21.330
You’ll what?!

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:24.130
Next time, “Cheers to 100-Star Jin.”

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:27.980
Cheers to 100-Star Jin

00:24:24.130 --> 00:24:26.000
Well, it’s quiz time!

00:24:26.000 --> 00:24:27.380
Let’s play up!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Aha ha ha!
I’m gonna get some airtime!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Hold it! We should be
the stars in this shot!!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
